      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Everett’s first public library opened in 1894 and moved into its permanent building in 1905, becoming a civic cornerstone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everett%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 834‑seat Historic Everett Theatre opened in 1901 on Colby Avenue and still hosts community theater, music, and film screenings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everett%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Waterfront Place, a hotel‑apartment‑restaurant complex, began construction in 2018 beside the public marina, reshaping downtown’s skyline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
